---
description: App Router pages, layouts, and client feature UI
globs: app/**/page.tsx,app/**/layout.tsx,app/**/loading.tsx,app/**/error.tsx,components/**/*.tsx,components/**/*.ts,hooks/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

- Page files stay thin. Example: `app/receive/page.tsx` loads data and renders `ReceiveScreen`; `app/production/page.tsx` renders `ProductionDashboard`.
- Feature UI lives in `components/features/<area>/`. Shell is `components/layout/`. Primitives are `components/ui/`, including `PageMain`, `ModalShell`, and `ScrollTable`.
- Role homes are `lib/utils/roleRouting.ts`. Edge middleware only checks that a page is signed in. Protected segment layouts and `app/page.tsx` call `guardFreshPage` on each navigation, including client transitions. The root layout also checks full document loads. Hiding a button is not the server check.

- After a ledger mutation, dispatch `freshloop-inventory-updated`. Rescue also dispatches `freshloop-kitchen-inbox`. Settings use `freshloop-settings-updated`.
- Optimistic stock UI uses `useOptimisticInventoryLevels` and must revert when the API returns no level or an error.
- Touch targets are at least `min-h-11`. Long names use `min-w-0 truncate`. Currency and quantities use `font-mono tabular-nums`.
- There are no Server Actions today. A control calls `fetch('/api/...')`. If a `"use server"` file is added later, extend `20-backend-boundaries.mdc` globs to that real path.
